branch: feature/intent-rule-induction

why: BACKLOG intent-rule-induction: the hand-written cues fire on 58.3%
  of messages and are 88.6-90.9% right where they fire, and their
  coverage grows with someone's patience. Induce them instead --
  literals are token presence (words and adjacent pairs), a rule is a
  conjunction, grown by FOIL gain on a growing set and pruned on a
  pruning set, per class, until no rule with two supporting rows is
  left -- so coverage grows with the corpus. Zero network, deterministic
  (a fixed split by index, ties by order). Measured on the TestModels
  held-out half beside `Patterns.meeting`: coverage, precision where
  fired, per class. A tier with the same train/score/classify contract;
  whether it enters the Router is the number's call, not this lane's.
